Z||000000||jake1852||07-02-2001||05:36 PM||||I have an 87 fiero SE. 55k orig miles. awesome condition, no rust at all. however, the car sat for the past few years untill i bought it. car overheats like crazy, the temperature guage goes nuts, flying up and down (i was told this is air in the cooling system), and the engine smokes from the exhaust manifold. this is what i have done so far with no luck.<P>changed plugs/wires<P>replaced gasket on valve cover<P>flushed the cooling sysem MILLIONS of times, at all different angles, i tried doing it with the engine revved at 2500 to get the air out, etc. i got it to not overheat for 40 minutes once doing this. <BR>changed both radiator cap and thermo housing cap.<P>i am no mechanic, but if someone would point me in the right direction i should be able to figure it out. i am ripping my hair out at this point, and if i cant figure it out, ill take it to a shop and get my wallet emptied.||||reg||4
Z||000001||jake1852||07-02-2001||05:41 PM||||oh i forgot one thing. do these cars have any balls whatsoever on the road? mine sure as hell doesnt! i am hoping that this is part of the problem. i also get very bad gas mileage (about 15-18)||||reg||2
Z||000002||Leadfoot||07-02-2001||05:44 PM||||Did you check to see if the thermal switch that controls the fan is working?  In other words, does your fan turn on when you reach temperatures around 235-240F?  Also, if you sit out in traffic and notice that the temp. is rising, hit A/C switch (this will turn on your fan) and see if the temp. goes down.  If your temp. goes down then it is a safe bet that your the thermal fan switch is out.  I have a brand new stock switch just sitting around if you want.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Leadfoot||07-02-2001||05:47 PM||||Do you have a 4 or a 6?<BR> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by jake1852:<BR><B>oh i forgot one thing. do these cars have any balls whatsoever on the road? mine sure as hell doesnt! i am hoping that this is part of the problem. i also get very bad gas mileage (about 15-18)</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>||||reg||1
Z||000004||jake1852||07-02-2001||05:57 PM||||leadfoot- yeah i checked my fan..and i have tried putting on the heat or a/c it didnt work. the car is a 4cyl||||reg||1
Z||000005||Leadfoot||07-02-2001||06:24 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by jake1852:<BR><B>the engine smokes from the exhaust manifold</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>If you see smoke your manifold might be cracked or the egr valve/tube maybe broken or cracked.  If the egr is defective then you will see a major decrease in performance and experience overheating.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000006||Leadfoot||07-02-2001||07:16 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by jake1852:<BR><B>leadfoot- yeah i checked my fan..and i have tried putting on the heat or a/c it didnt work. the car is a 4cyl</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Sorry for the multiple post.  My connection is kinda screwy.  Anyway, the fan should turn on if the a/c is on.  Looks like you may have a bad fan motor.<BR>||||reg||1
