Z||000008||prtzlboy||07-02-2001||08:24 PM||||Could be a sticky thermostat.  I'd get a new one just in case; they're way cheap.  As far as the smoke goes, someone mentioned the egr.  Is your "service engine soon" (or "check engine", but I think the '87s had ses) light coming on?  If so check the codes.||||reg||1
Z||000009||Fierowrecker||07-02-2001||08:36 PM||||Hey Jake!<BR>You have a problem that requires a little finnesse...<BR>Have you the time and inclination to do a little work?<BR>First, check the water pump, it sounds like it isn't pumping the water through the system...<BR>They are notorious for failing by having the rotor fall off...<BR>DO NOT ACCEPT A PLASTIC IMPELLER ON THE REPLACEMENT!!!<P>Where are you? If there is a club around, some of the members would help you out...<BR>It is easy to get discuraged, but with help, you should soon have a fine running car...<BR>crash...<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000010||V8Fiero||07-02-2001||08:36 PM||||Had a similar problem with my 86se. Fresh rebuilt engine (supposedly) and it had sat for two + yrs. Same symptom. Tried all this, new thermostat, flushing out system, different radiator. Turned out to be the water pump. Check the weep hole on the bottome of the pump to see if its leaking. I would suggest replacing anyway. Only around $25 at the local parts store.<P>Scott||||reg||1
Z||000011||jake1852||07-02-2001||08:43 PM||||water pump seems fine.weep hole is fine and if i put my ear to the metal pipes under the car i can hear water rushing. got a new thermo too. didnt work.<BR>i think it is air in the lines, cause of the short bursts of overheating. it doesnt gradually overheat, its really sudden and lasts for a few minutes, goes down, then does it all over again. if i downshift and step on it, it usually cools down for a few minutes. <BR>sorry for my ignorance, but what is an egr?<BR>oh and for the guy who wanted to know,im located in NE Conn.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000012||Seanh||07-02-2001||09:10 PM||||EGR is Exhaust Gas Recurculation. I don't know jack squat about the 4 bangers, I'v only worked with one and I just pulled it from the car and thats about it. If you ask me, you should do a compression test. You could have a blown head gasket. It would definatly result in overheating, lots of smoking, and horrible performance. I know, I'v done so many Fiero head gaskets I could now do them in 2 days, blindfolded, with one hand tied behind my back.<P>When you have your thermostat cap off, and the car running, can you see the water moving? If so, chances are your pump is working correctly. Perhaps your radiator is shot? Do you loose coolant? Does your coolant puke up after you shut the car off maybe? Does the car run ok? Maybe, just maybe, your temp guage is actually the problem, and the engine might not be overheating at all. You smoking could be many other things, not related to overheating, but most likly causing your poor performance.||||reg||1
Z||000013||jake1852||07-02-2001||09:33 PM||||yeah i had my radiator checked, it flows at 15 gallons per minute.the car does run great (there is a small tick, not sure what it is) the temp guage is fine. the car does get hot. thanks people for all the advice.||||reg||1
Z||000014||Phil||07-02-2001||10:03 PM||||Make sure you have the right kind of rad cap- Fieros use a non-vented cap contrary to what some of the fitment catalogs say, also make sure that the hose from the rad to the overflow tank is not clogged. Just ran into this after installing the engine into the wife's car. I had a bunch of trouble getting the system burped. You do know the proper procedure I assume.||||reg||1
Z||000015||maryjane||07-03-2001||01:43 AM||||Jake, I had a very similar problem with a 4 cyl. Temp would cycle up & down fairly rapidly. Ran fine without the thermostat, but the thermo wasn't the problem. The fan relay would not close while driving and sometimes just sitting. The fan would come on when I was checking it but not always on the road when the temp senso told it to. I took too long to find the problem and ended up with a cracked head. They won't stand repeated overheating. Wish I could offer more help-good luck<BR>Don & Jane<P>------------------<BR>84 SE 2.5<BR>not slow not fast-just halfast||||reg||1
Z||000016||b lo 0||07-03-2001||02:39 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by jake1852:<BR><B>oh i forgot one thing. do these cars have any balls whatsoever on the road? mine sure as hell doesnt! i am hoping that this is part of the problem. i also get very bad gas mileage (about 15-18)</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>The Iron Duke was an OK motor, but was REALLY REALLY slow!  (Sorry for the overexaggeration).  Point is, don't expect balls-to-the-wall performance with anything short of a modified 2.8l V6.  Not sure about the gas mileage,tho.  I've got the 2.8.  The Duke has, like, what...80, 90 hp?  (Help me out, guys) while the V6 rolled out of the factory at 145 hp.<BR><P>------------------<BR>'85 GT (in progress)  <BR>titled ICE-plates B LO 0 <BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.angelfire.com/ga3/audioimagery/ice.gif">     <BR>Go to <A HREF="http://www.audioimagery.i-p.com" TARGET=_blank>www.audioimagery.i-p.com</A>  !!!<P><A HREF="http://clubs.excite.com/welcome/main?cid=.zXb1DJ1lsCL&aid=22&auth=" TARGET=_blank>Pontiac Fiero Owner's Club</A>-Pics, Videos and More-Or Post your Own||||reg||1
Z||000017||jake1852||07-03-2001||08:46 AM||||phil: <BR>i have a non-vented cap on the thermostat housing, but on the radiator, i have a regular cap. are you saying i need a nonvented on both?<BR>when i burp the system, i park it in my driveway (nose raised in the air) pull the radiator cap off, run the car at 2500 rpm and fill the radiator everytime the level drops. is this the right way?<BR>thanks<P>------------------<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000018||Carrolles||07-03-2001||09:04 AM||||When you burp the system the nose needs to be DOWN slightly.  I park mine in my driveway with the front wheels in the curb when I burp it.  If you burp it with the nose up it will create a high point that will trap an air bubble.<P>Remove the radiator cap and the thermostat housing cap.  Fill from the t-stat housing until coolant starts to come out of the radiator cap.<P>Replace the radiator cap.  Continue to fill from the t-stat housing.  Start the engine and let it circulate for a while to get the air out.  You'll probably be able to add a bit more coolant as the air escapes.  Shut it down and install the t-stat and its cap.<P>Fill the overflow bottle to the recommended level.<P>Both caps need to be Non-vented.<P>A vented radiator cap will let coolant siphon out through the overflow bottle if the nose is slightly down when the car cools off.<P>Hope this helps,<P>Carroll||||reg||1
Z||000019||Loki||07-03-2001||10:48 AM||||The way I have always filled the coolant is as follows..<BR>  1) jack the ass end in the air<BR>  2)  remove thermostat hoseing cap and thermostat<BR>  3) Fill with water then coolant (or mix whatever)<BR>  4) let stand till no more bubbles come out..I sometimes squeeze the  rubber hoses to make the fluid go through em all<BR>  5) no more bubbles, close it all up and enjoy..<P><P>------------------<BR>Loki<BR>ICQ# 16477998||||reg||1
Z||000020||Dave Gunsul||07-03-2001||11:48 AM||||I would check the oil to see if there's coolant in it. I really hope that it's an air bubble in the cooling system but I think<BR>you've got a blown head gasket.<P>------------------<BR>Dave Gunsul<BR>N.I.F.E. member<BR>86 GT modified<BR>85 SE daily driver<p>[This message has been edited by Dave Gunsul (edited 07-03-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000021||jake1852||07-03-2001||06:54 PM||||thank you guys for your instructions. i will do it tomorrow. <P>oh- i dont have a blown head gasket. no oil in the water, no water in the oil, no steam from the exhaust.<P>thanks again, all<P>------------------<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000022||jake1852||07-14-2001||12:29 PM||||well, i did everything y'all told me to do, and i am still ****ed. i did manage to fix the smoking problem and the "ball-less" problem, but the overheating still gets me. one thing i did not do, is find a non-vented cap for the radiator. the best anyone could do for me was to give me a 16lb vented cap. nobody has any non vented ones anymore. does anyone know where i could get one? and are you sure that it needs to be non-vented? because if it is, doesnt that eliminate the overflow? please help me out here guys.||||reg||8
Z||000023||fierohoho||07-14-2001||01:10 PM||||Ok, I have a thought. Could your temp sensor be bad? <P>It may be that it is registering wrong. <P>You sound like you've done all you can so I would replace the gage temp sensor, they do tend to go bad.<P>My '84 2.5 had sat for 10 years and the guy I bought it from couldn't remember why his wife had stopped driving it, after some clean up I got it running and the only thing I found wrong was a bad temp sensor had been replaced with the wrong sensor.<P>I put in the right new sensor and problem solved. <P>Good luck<P>------------------<BR>'84 SE 2.5l<BR>'85 Coupe 2.5l now getting a 3800<BR>'86 SE 2.5l||||reg||1
Z||000024||Mach10||07-14-2001||01:55 PM||||Mine did that. Caused by low coolant. I'd top it off, and it'd drain in a couple of weeks. Turns out it was the water pump. The weep hole would start to squirt at high RPMs, so it wasn't noticeable on the driveway, and by the time I'd get home, coasting to my spot either at home, or parking lot at work, nothing would come out of the pump. My coolant would trickle out until my reservoir was empty. Then I'd get a huge embolism in my cooling system, and my temp gauge would swing like it was listening to music. Are you losing coolant? does your level go down? bear in mind that I lost all of mine on the highway. I never found ANY on my driveway, or parking space.<BR>Another bad thing to happen is a waterpump malfunction, where a leak starts taking in air, and air-locking to pump. Still pumps, but VERY WEAKLY. Perhaps enough to make sounds, but not to move coolant. Either way, pull the pump off, man! ||||reg||14
Z||000025||jake1852||07-14-2001||02:37 PM||||you know, i think you are right! i did notice that my overflow tank was pretty low, and i had filled it. hmm...i think i will change the pump. if its not that, then, well...i will just kill myself...lol||||reg||1
