Z||000033||HummelHund||07-24-2001||04:49 PM||||I'm not sure about the overheating problem, but as for the smoke, check to make sure your PCV is in the right way. I stuck mine in turned around backwards, and well, that won't work. Maybe I'm the only one stupid enough to do something like that, but it caused TONS of smoke to pour from what seemed like every orifice in the car (including the air intake vent, ever seen a smoke breathing Fiero?). As for the overheating thing, I say take it somewhere to get the coolant flushed an refilled and then blame the problems on them.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><BR><P>------------------<BR>Sean W.<BR>'84 SE 2M4 WS6 (restoration project to become daily driver)<BR>'84 Sport Coupe ($150 running car)||||reg||1
Z||000034||prtzlboy||07-24-2001||06:50 PM||||you mentioned ticking before, and I don't know if you got that taken care of or not, but it could be a cracked manifold.||||reg||1
